    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "B•0•A•C\nintroduces\nthe newest,\nfastest airliner\nin the world\nComet\nJETLINER\nBRITISH OVERSEAS AIRWAYS CORPORATION",
      "B.O.A.C. Comet Jetliner\nHOW THE TURBO-JET ENGINE WORKS\nThe turbo jet engine gulps air in through the nose,\nspire the compressor. Finding no obstacle behind\ncompresses it, then feeds it into the combustion\nthe turbine, the hot blast expands quickly, turning\nchamber where it is mixed with fuel and ignited.\nheat and pressure into velocity, and rushes out the\nThe result is a blast of hot gass which escapes\ntail pipe, creating the thrust which pushes the Comet\ntoward the rear, spinning the turbine which in turn\nthrough the sky at high speed.\nFLAME TUBE\nCOMPRESSOR\nTUNHIRIE\nAIR\nJET PIPE\nDelicious complimentary meals and mealtime drinks served\nduring flight by the stewards and stewarden.\n8 of the Comer's 30\npassengers are accom-\nmodated in this forward\ncabin, where there are\ntwo tables, with two pairs\nof facing seats to each.\nIndividual reading lights,\ndark blue carpets and\nupholstery, and silver-grey\nwalls and celling give a\nrestful effect.\nB•O-A•C\nregular air services\nto these\ndestinations\nGREAT BRITAIN SPAIN\nPORTUGAL • ITALY: SWITZERLAND\nU.S.A.\nBERMUDA CANADA\nBAHAMAS WEST INDIES\nSOUTH AMERICA MIDDLE EAST\nWEST AFRICA EAST AFRICA\nSOUTH AFRICA PAKISTAN\nINDIA\nCEYLON\nAUSTRALIA\nNEW ZEALAND • PAR EAST • JAPAN\nintroduces\nthe newest,\nfastest airliner\nin the world\nYOU CAN BOOK THROUGH\nNO BOOKING FEE\nB.O.A.C. TAKES GOOD CARE OF YOU\nComet\nJETLINER\nOVERS\nCORFORITION\nBRITISH\nCORFORATION",
      "FACTS ABOUT THE\nComet\nThe Comet Jetliner marks a milestone\nin passenger transport.\nIt is the world's first jetliner and\nis the first to go into regular service. In it,\npassengers enter a new era of effortless,\ncomfortable, fast and sure flying.\nThis superb example of British\nengineering skill is yet another triumph\nfor the de Havilland Aircraft and\nEngine Companies.\nCruising at nearly 500 miles per hour,\nit is half as fast again as any\nother airliner now in regular service\nand the timetable will show the\nextent to which flying times have\nbeen slashed.\nWhen the Comet is\nin full operation, no place on B.O.A.C.\nroutes should ever be more than two\ndays away from the point of\ndeparture.\nAll feeling of motion is lost in the\nsmooth clear air of the Comet's\nnormal operational altitude.\nThe lack of vibration gives the illusion\nof being suspended in space while a\nfascinating panorama unfolds\nitself through the cabin window.\nThe Comet's galley is a miracle of compactness and\nefficiency.\nEquipment includes two tabletops,\na sink, removable waste bin, electric oven\nand urn, and cold storage cabinet.\nFresh, filtered water is\navallabic al all times from\nthe drinking fountain,\nconvementy locateo 311\nof the main cabin on the\nstarboard side.\nFront passenger cabin\nMain passenger cabin\nRear baggage hold\n4 Men's room\n5 To men's toilets\n6 Ladies' toilet\n7 Ladies' dressing room\n13\n8 Main entrance and vestibule\n9 Wardrobe\nFreight hold\nSteward\nDiplomatic nail locker\nPantry\n14 Freight hold\n18\n\" Picture\" windows of\ngenerous dimensions are\nnited in the passenger cabins.\nIn the main cabin there is a\nwindow adjacent to each\npair of seats.\nThe Slumberseats fitted\nin the aircraft are\ncasily adjustable and\nsupremely comfortable\nin any position.\nThey\nare probably the most\nrestful chairs in the\nworld.\nNavigator\nCaptain\nFirst Officer-Engineer\nRadio Officer\nCrew entry door\nSteward (s)\nA built-in book-case is\nprovided for the fight\nibrary which includes\nfiction and non-fiction,\nreference books and\ncurrent weekly and\nmonthly magazines."
    ],
